{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And there was in Jeshurun a king, when the heads of the people assembled, etc.</b> — meaning, that the existence of a king over Israel requires that it come about through the assembling of the heads of the people together, as they said of blessed memory (Tosefta Sanhedrin ch. 3): they may not appoint a king except by decision of a court of seventy-one. And this is what is intended by the phrase ״heads of the people,״ and in his saying ״together the tribes of Israel״ — that there must be a public accepted by them." "<b>Further,</b> it may be explained that since he stated nearby that the Torah is what rules over us, as it says (Proverbs 8:6) ״נְגִידִים אֲדַבֵּר,״ therefore he concluded ״and there was in Jeshurun a king״ — meaning, the existence of a king over Israel will come about if the heads of the people assemble and request a king; then is when he will be king. And this is his saying ״when the heads of the people assembled״ etc. — then is when there will be a king in Jeshurun, apart from the Torah. And similarly we find that the appointment of a king over Israel took place in this manner, as it is written in Samuel (I Samuel 8:4) ״וַיִּתְקַבְּצוּ כָל זִקְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל וַיָּבוֹאוּ אֶל שְׁמוּאֵל, etc. שִׂימָה לָּנוּ מֶלֶךְ לְשָׁפְטֵנוּ״ — and this itself is the phrase ״when they assembled״ etc. But without this, the Torah alone will be king over Israel, and this is what the prophet said to them (I Samuel 12:12) ״וַה׳ אֱלֹהֵיכֶם מַלְכְּכֶם״ — which is the Torah, for it is entirely the Name of the Holy One, blessed be He." "<b>Or perhaps</b> it is for this reason that he hinted by means of the word ״וַיְהִי,״ which denotes distress (Megillah 10b), as it is written there (I Samuel 8:6) ״וַיֵּרַע הַדָּבָר בְּעֵינֵי שְׁמוּאֵל כַּאֲשֶׁר אָמְרוּ תְּנָה לָּנוּ מֶלֶךְ לְשָׁפְטֵנוּ,״ and it is written (ibid. v. 7) ״וַיֹּאמֶר ה׳, etc. כִּי אוֹתִי מָאֲסוּ מִמְּלוֹךְ עֲלֵיהֶם.״ And concerning this Moses prophesied and said ״וַיְהִי״ etc." "<b>Further,</b> he hinted that the kingdom of Israel will endure when Israel assembles their heads together and they are not each on their own, for through this there will be a cause that the tribes of Israel will be joined together. And when Israel is in this state, behold they are at the height of the category of success, and their kingdom will have an existence of permanence. Go out and learn: from the day the hearts were divided and the kingdoms were split, what came of their hands? And this is the cause of the calves of Jeroboam and those who followed him, for the root of destruction is separation, and the vessel that holds blessing is peace (Uktzin 3:12) and the unification of hearts."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:22:04.782851304Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}